    "topics": [
      "skills",
      "evolution",
      "agents"
    ],
    "depth": "source-reviewed",
    "summary": "Offer a spec-driven coding bundle or importer rather than adopting Spec Kit's directory conventions as the entire harness architecture. Reuse format adapters and artifact templates where suitable. Enforce required state transitions in the task engine, with policy-controlled overrides recorded as decisions. Evaluate cross-platform paths, command escaping, hook failures, stale checklists, and end-to-end requirement-to-test traceability. Preserve the user's chosen workflow and allow a lightweight task path where a full specification adds little value.",
    "word_count": 341
  },
  {
